# Fernhollow: duplicate jobs follow-up

Monday, October 5, 2026 at 09:02 · 16 min

## Attendees

- Tom Becker
- Shreyas
- Owen Price

## Notes

#### Decisions

- Fernhollow receives a service credit of one month of fees for all sixty technicians ($2,700 at $45 per technician), applied to the November invoice, covering the three double dispatches.
- Owen and his two dispatch leads are added to Deino's release-notes email list.
- Deino will send Fernhollow a notice forty-eight hours before any release that touches calendar sync; the office manager is left off that list.
- Shreyas will deliver a written postmortem to Fernhollow by Friday 9 October.
- Fernhollow will not join the Calendar Sync v2 beta and will wait for general availability.
- Any support ticket about duplicate or missing jobs is now high priority by default.

#### Key facts

- **How many duplicate jobs were removed from Fernhollow's account?** One hundred and thirty-two, created between 15 September and the previous Friday; the cleanup ran on Saturday morning.
- **How many jobs were dispatched twice, and which ones?** Three: the furnace service on Alder Road (22 Sept), the water heater on Pine Street (29 Sept) and the boiler check at the Brookside apartments (1 Oct).
- **What did the double dispatches cost Fernhollow?** About four hundred dollars per wasted call-out, roughly twelve hundred dollars for the three.
- **What caused the duplicate jobs?** The v1.4 release (15 September) changed event matching and stopped looking at which occurrence of a recurring series an event is, so a single moved occurrence was treated as a new event and a second job was created.
- **Why was Fernhollow hit harder than other customers?** Fernhollow books most maintenance as recurring events and its dispatchers move individual visits much more often than most customers.
- **How big is the service credit and how was it calculated?** $2,700: one month of fees for sixty technicians at $45 per technician, applied to the November invoice.
- **When does the permanent fix go out?** Tuesday 6 October 2026; a temporary guard has been in place since Friday night.
- **How much advance notice will Fernhollow get for sync changes?** Forty-eight hours before any release that touches calendar sync, on top of the general release-notes email.
- **What additional monitoring is Deino adding?** An alert if the number of jobs sync creates for any one customer suddenly spikes, so Deino notices within hours.
- **Why can't Fernhollow stay on the old version of sync?** Deino runs one version for everyone, so pinning a customer to an old version is not possible; the 48-hour notice is the chance to raise concerns.
- **Did any duplicate jobs reach Fernhollow's invoicing?** Two duplicates marked complete by a technician ended up as draft invoices in the QuickBooks export on 28 September; they are flagged in column F and Owen will have them voided.

